a","guid":"Lh6QoXwYSAyP4Q8nFQQN2A","children":[]},{"id":"176","parent":"174","text":"Discordancia clínica / test / imagen","guid":"pnIX3ZJ4RhOwzfyACDlXeg","children":[]},{"id":"177","parent":"174","text":"Selección para ensayos / terapias modificadoras","guid":"_bAcdH50Sv2RS3DKw3RQKQ","children":[]},{"id":"178","parent":"174","text":"Estudios familiares con consejería genética","guid":"m-MNCkxJSTetSv_7MndP_A","children":[]}]},{"id":"179","parent":"162","text":"NO en asintomáticos (tema ético)","guid":"RMB8GKotReOcl0vPGAtB_w","children":[]},{"id":"180","parent":"162","text":"Stepwise approach Altuna 2025 → cribado cognitivo + FR + neuroimagen + plasma p-tau 217 jerarquizado en APS","guid":"I8oA4Y0lSyOgYV5FMeGwnQ","children":[]}]},{"id":"181","parent":"0","text":"Prevención — 14 factores modificables (Lancet 2024, Livingston)","guid":"hFeU7s-ASDCvzk74Swy5ug","children":[{"id":"182","parent":"181","text":"Hasta 45% de las demencias son PREVENIBLES","guid":"-O-C4EZgToSbtqXaDPH73w","children":[]},{"id":"183","parent":"181","text":"En LATAM/Chile alcanza >50%","guid":"Dv3KjGH8R5CuuSKcQRKWTQ","children":[]},{"id":"184","parent":"181","text":"Vida temprana (<18)","guid":"iwapNywRT9OzlJ9OL0X4MA","children":[{"id":"185","parent":"184","text":"Bajo nivel educacional","guid":"hQVOMLByQcCDFt3C3Bh5Mw","children":[]}]},{"id":"186","parent":"181","text":"Vida media (18-65)","guid":"htXjurFbTr2HI65rm_t_FA","children":[{"id":"187","parent":"186","text":"Pérdida auditiva","guid":"OfFJEoOvTy2oEf6PB44vPQ","children":[]},{"id":"188","parent":"186","text":"HTA","guid":"2umIgUEKQTq0fZaxFmGhqA","children":[]},{"id":"189","parent":"186","text":"Obesidad","guid":"5mn05qqaQBOyu0w6UtqlIQ","children":[]},{"id":"190","parent":"186","text":"Exceso de alcohol","guid":"i-5UWsIlSHi10m-zznNyzg","children":[]},{"id":"191","parent":"186","text":"Trauma craneoencefálico","guid":"1REg5W3pSwWChOz_pPfhew","children":[]},{"id":"192","parent":"186","text":"LDL elevado (factor nuevo Lancet 2024)","guid":"IT9C_UXpSd2eaMpAuFVX3w","children":[]}]},{"id":"193","parent":"181","text":"Vida tardía (>65)","guid":"P44ifVaGSY692YbTaRC5gw","children":[{"id":"194","parent":"193","text":"Tabaquismo","guid":"XhAmzN_lTBaVtr3W0Q4ZQA","children":[]},{"id":"195","parent":"193","text":"Depresión","guid":"ReEx_MTZQYC_issPZiftaA","children":[]},{"id":"196","parent":"193","text":"Inactividad física","guid":"RT0eInwsSuKOfBqTrdLqsg","children":[]},{"id":"197","parent":"193","text":"Aislamiento social","guid":"G_y95hBAS0K9BZOp4_x00A","children":[]},{"id":"198","parent":"193","text":"Diabetes","guid":"KFNl1LjJSYuqY7na3IM1Ew","children":[]},{"id":"199","parent":"193","text":"Contaminación ambiental","guid":"ItEG75rFTziBaNZWyBdG6w","children":[]},{"id":"200","parent":"193","text":"Pérdida de visión (factor nuevo Lancet 2024)","guid":"lPbFNiqDTg-aA8VIWU5S7g","children":[]}]},{"id":"201","parent":"181","text":"Estudios clave","guid":"XhGtMgakQfOJM7hmIL2ZEQ","children":[{"id":"202","parent":"201","text":"CARDIA → variabilidad glucosa edad media → ↑ riesgo demencia temprana","guid":"9q8c4rN4QfuXxsISvspxag","children":[]},{"id":"203","parent":"201","text":"SPRINT MIND → control estricto PA edad media → ↓ 19% demencia a edades tardías","guid":"Ev0CA0IwS6ehh_2fuTpIfw","children":[]},{"id":"204","parent":"201","text":"Reserva cognitiva → misma carga amiloide pero MÁS educación = MENOS manifestación","guid":"L35PROwMTcCsz5TR9VZwtw","children":[]}]},{"id":"205","parent":"181","text":"AHA Brain Health Agenda (Lazar Stroke 2021) → 7 áreas para APS: PA, glucosa, lípidos, dieta, actividad, peso, no fumar","guid":"yVHzbLGjRWSR1MmXva838Q","children":[]},{"id":"206","parent":"181","text":"Reuben JAMA Intern Med 2024 → revisión narrativa prevención + tratamiento; mensajes centrales para clínicos","guid":"zwTBkF67T_OBazazV63jHA","children":[]}]},{"id":"207","parent":"0","text":"Rasgos clínicos por tipo de demencia","guid":"cdFzJbi6RxCdqtLCMavD3Q","children":[{"id":"208","parent":"207","text":"Alzheimer típico (McKhann NIA-AA 2011) → insidioso; memoria episódica (fallo precoz)","guid":"Ga0-tRFLRguVMy0qq7eLDg","children":[]},{"id":"209","parent":"207","text":"Demencia vascular (O'Brien Lancet 2015) → escalonado; antecedente/imagen vascular; disfunción ejecutiva, subcortical","guid":"LjDSTiQYSTeqRd92Q6IqXA","children":[{"id":"210","parent":"209","text":"Goodall JACC 2026 → terapia emergente (control vascular, anti-amiloide, terapia hipertensiva intensiva)","guid":"WZpwhTfRRwCyypjgVessRw","children":[]}]},{"id":"211","parent":"207","text":"Demencia por cuerpos de Lewy / DLB (McKeith Neurology 2017) → fluctuante; alucinaciones visuales estructuradas; parkinsonismo; hipersensibilidad neuroléptica","guid":"RBKX3TPHSk-ByUwTkEWp4g","children":[]},{"id":"212","parent":"207","text":"Demencia asociada a Parkinson (PDD) → lento; parkinsonismo ≥5a antes del cognitivo","guid":"bHS4YEVCQQSJ4ewQeWcsIg","children":[]},{"id":"213","parent":"207","text":"Frontotemporal (DFT) → variable; cambios conductuales o alteración del lenguaje precoz, antes que memoria","guid":"2ETedRo6Tw2XF_THkU2JqQ","children":[]},{"id":"214","parent":"207","text":"\"Regla del año\" DLB vs PDD","guid":"ze_zURanRhu3ErIv3fk4Jw","children":[{"id":"215","parent":"214","text":"Cognitivo en 1er año del parkinsonismo → DLB","guid":"iswDxTnQQwmiwBJ36xjnrA","children":[]},{"id":"216","parent":"214","text":"Cognitivo ≥5 años después → PDD","guid":"ywtqCKMBT3WIXnO-xN8V0A","children":[]}]},{"id":"217","parent":"207","text":"Petersen Neurology 2018 → guía MCI: definición, evaluación, manejo","guid":"YShC7S6NTsejNGzsVidlnA","children":[]}]},{"id":"218","parent":"0","text":"Impacto cardiovascular del DCL (Jamil JACC 2025)","guid":"q58U3OdzTHiGlBvvEKX5Wg","children":[{"id":"219","parent":"218","text":"DCL aumenta morbi-mortalidad CV (peor adherencia, peor autocuidado)","guid":"c2bLN7hSSOil70Rd1ECBZw","children":[]},{"id":"220","parent":"218","text":"Intervenciones CV (estatinas, anti-HTA, anticoagulación) deben individualizarse en DCL/demencia","guid":"7iyHfp3lQ_6LzueT0fe5Ew","children":[]},{"id":"221","parent":"218","text":"Mensaje clínico → la cognición es vital signo cardiovascular en geriatría","guid":"4EIIlQ6RR2W184rm9ibxAA","children":[]}]},{"id":"222","parent":"0","text":"Banderas rojas — estudio urgente / derivación","guid":"f_oFJawPR2GGUDYbniHYjA","children":[{"id":"223","parent":"222","text":"Inicio <60a","guid":"9V108dO-TVaBM7_VXhxPzQ","children":[]},{"id":"224","parent":"222","text":"Progresión rápida (semanas-meses)","guid":"g6WQ1F5wR-yrW1E8rGvVjw","children":[]},{"id":"225","parent":"222","text":"Crisis epilépticas, déficit focales, signos piramidales","guid":"Ja1dIx6KSsqzWt6_yt0Bbw","children":[]},{"id":"226","parent":"222","text":"Fiebre, pérdida peso, signos sistémicos","guid":"Wg2PLtsVS76I-YzmjtNypg","children":[]},{"id":"227","parent":"222","text":"Inmunosupresión o antecedentes oncológicos","guid":"MM1xfQZGSeyrwHf_zY_qvw","children":[]},{"id":"228","parent":"222","text":"Delirium persistente sin causa clara","guid":"w_ZwzkH5Q46mCdMrgwv8dg","children":[]},{"id":"229","parent":"222","text":"Pensar en → demencias rápidamente progresivas, tumores, encefalitis","guid":"lsHxt4U9T9OUiAsrkeJvuw","children":[]}]},{"id":"230","parent":"0","text":"Algoritmo diagnóstico ambulatorio (síntesis Nettig)","guid":"casbIJGvTj6d71G8Wi7NtQ","children":[{"id":"231","parent":"230","text":"1. Sospecha clínica (paciente o informante)","guid":"CKuTLN7GReOYHkucj0fEIg","children":[]},{"id":"232","parent":"230","text":"2. Anamnesis dirigida + VGI con informante","guid":"Wjx2HlosQBWyYv5H8rWNrQ","children":[]},{"id":"233","parent":"230","text":"3. Funcionalidad (Barthel + Lawton + fragilidad)","guid":"DS45AcTDRBKVOOHjxKU4yQ","children":[]},{"id":"234","parent":"230","text":"4. Test de cribado: MoCA o Mini-Cog o RUDAS si baja escolaridad","guid":"N5a0sbSbRsan6Ilug0XReQ","children":[]},{"id":"235","parent":"230","text":"5. Laboratorio básico: NUNCA olvidar TSH + B12","guid":"qb8_P-0gTs6uGJuPkW6dxA","children":[]},{"id":"236","parent":"230","text":"6. Neuroimagen: TAC (GES Chile) o RM","guid":"HO2ZKnOxQumGRpmERdblCg","children":[]},{"id":"237","parent":"230","text":"7. Diagnóstico probable + plan de manejo APS","guid":"dm326XacR06IPeE1MPpc_Q","children":[]},{"id":"238","parent":"230","text":"8. Atípicos/dudosos → derivar a unidades de memoria","guid":"U6CJe4F1Q8y6cmKQPdetow","children":[]}]},{"id":"239","parent":"0","text":"Preguntas Autoestudio (oficiales Dra. Natalia Nettig)","guid":"DAuod_2uSV-ngLyYH2jWBw","children":[{"id":"240","parent":"239","text":"1. Explique las diferencias clínicas y funcionales fundamentales entre envejecimiento cognitivo normal, deterioro cognitivo leve (DCL) y demencia según las guías NIA-AA y AAN","guid":"VLrRpTpvQleY-uAYHBdJ_Q","children":[]},{"id":"241","parent":"239","text":"2. Describa el marco AT(N) propuesto por NIA-AA para la enfermedad de Alzheimer: qué representa cada letra, qué biomarcadores se utilizan y en qué contextos clínicos puede ser útil","guid":"GDbMGdsyRTSdbGe_YQiOew","children":[]},{"id":"242","parent":"239","text":"3. Plantee un algoritmo práctico de evaluación ambulatoria de un paciente mayor con sospecha de deterioro cognitivo, incluyendo: historia, exploración, pruebas de cribado, laboratorio, neuroimagen y criterios para pedir evaluación neuropsicológica y biomarcadores","guid":"e-YMKVpOQgWbC3iBxK_3rw","children":[]},{"id":"243","parent":"239","text":"4. Compare las presentaciones clínicas típicas de enfermedad de Alzheimer, demencia vascular, demencia con cuerpos de Lewy y demencia frontotemporal (dominio inicial afectado, curso, hallazgos clave en la exploración y en neuroimagen)","guid":"6xOykmSrQkmNY9ZTtoimYQ","children":[]},{"id":"244","parent":"239","text":"5. Enumere al menos 5 causas potencialmente reversibles de deterioro cognitivo en la persona mayor y describa qué pruebas básicas solicitaría para descartarlas","guid":"VWavDrzyT1KpWdRwxrv4Xg","children":[]},{"id":"245","parent":"239","text":"6. Analice los criterios clínicos para derivar a un paciente con deterioro cognitivo desde atención primaria/consulta general a una unidad de memoria, e indique qué información mínima debería acompañar a la derivación","guid":"F05DA5q8S_6QUiWUQAQw5g","children":[]}]},{"id":"246","parent":"0","text":"Evidencia complementaria (papers oficiales)","guid":"sC9Dv2mTSlOVbrI-LX656w","children":[{"id":"247","parent":"246","text":"Frisoni Lancet 2025 → nuevo panorama del diagnóstico de Alzheimer (biomarcadores plasmáticos)","guid":"S_s_4tJ5TxW_zZj1lhGcbg","children":[]},{"id":"248","parent":"246","text":"Altuna Sci Rep 2025 → algoritmo escalonado para APS: cribado → FR → neuroimagen → plasma p-tau 217","guid":"CWl5y4SPSLW8uRbcS_WHmQ","children":[]},{"id":"249","parent":"246","text":"USPSTF JAMA 2020 → evidencia insuficiente para tamizaje universal en asintomáticos","guid":"JzDoXfwvQvKYtknPDYetIw","children":[]},{"id":"250","parent":"246","text":"Goodall JACC 2026 → terapias actuales y emergentes para deterioro cognitivo vascular","guid":"ySehgEwrSnuczN0Fh0mYAA","children":[]},{"id":"251","parent":"246","text":"Putignano ELDERCARE 2024 → detección temprana en >60a","guid":"kyhaSbB0RFCyr2J4s7R5cg","children":[]},{"id":"252","parent":"246","text":"Lazar Stroke 2021 (AHA) → agenda de cerebro sano para APS (7 áreas)","guid":"z-VMuvF5T06YHZje6LcPGA","children":[]},{"id":"253","parent":"246","text":"Livingston Lancet 2024 → 14 factores prevenibles, 45% atribuible; nuevos factores: visión, LDL elevado","guid":"zz5Z0dzDTOKGbn5VxYTRgg","children":[]},{"id":"254","parent":"246","text":"Reuben JAMA Intern Med 2024 → prevención + tratamiento de demencia, revisión narrativa","guid":"ZhjfKta2QmurpDgYENAbZA","children":[]},{"id":"255","parent":"246","text":"McKhann NIA-AA 2011 → criterios diagnósticos de Alzheimer","guid":"udJfzFlpQTimMh28yMKlmw","children":[]},{"id":"256","parent":"246","text":"Jamil JACC 2025 → impacto del DCL sobre enfermedad CV","guid":"FW8iWm-nTHGBw4rvfDvxRA","children":[]},{"id":"257","parent":"246","text":"Petersen Neurology 2018 → guía MCI: práctica y seguimiento","guid":"hNgFWm-uS0mUXCGdqHiORw","children":[]},{"id":"258","parent":"246","text":"O'Brien Lancet 2015 → demencia vascular: revisión integral","guid":"PRHu2FWeSpOzwUnLC4M5CQ","children":[]},{"id":"259","parent":"246","text":"Ancelin 3-City Study (PLoS One 2009) → BZD aumentan deterioro cognitivo","guid":"DSpirRsOTLy0sDm-SLbREg","children":[]},{"id":"260","parent":"246","text":"Inouye Lancet 2014 → delirium predictor de demencia futura","guid":"vXbx4UkeQ3-4enzHM2rsyA","children":[]},{"id":"261","parent":"246","text":"Nasreddine 2005 → MoCA original","guid":"QAOJM0kwSnKxZ_HJmaRkzA","children":[]},{"id":"262","parent":"246","text":"Zarit 1980 → escala de carga del cuidador","guid":"cNqe4FYhSBy_2bQKcxX2cw","children":[]},{"id":"263","parent":"246","text":"Jack NIA-AA Research Framework 2018 → marco ATN","guid":"Rb533ZB3R822kjmLz3Ksjw","children":[]},{"id":"264","parent":"246","text":"Dubois 2016 → diagnóstico oportuno en Alzheimer","guid":"dTivxxEPRVK8y-m9Ygu6yA","children":[]},{"id":"265","parent":"246","text":"McKeith Neurology 2017 → criterios DLB","guid":"NwwQWnzhScirXG005HvP7w","children":[]},{"id":"266","parent":"246","text":"Fazekas 1987 → escala de hiperintensidades de sustancia blanca","guid":"Jm60O9TJSmK93gpv42n1uw","children":[]},{"id":"267","parent":"246","text":"Wardlaw Lancet Neurol 2013 → estándares cSVD imaging","guid":"bGYwcUCvR7SfSqgRujgqzg","children":[]},{"id":"268","parent":"246","text":"MINSAL Chile → Plan Nacional Demencia 2017 + GES-85 2019","guid":"Vd7F8YIjRRyH2jXjqdwUPg","children":[]}]},{"id":"269","parent":"0","text":"Perlas Clínicas","guid":"2xZwSftfS9O0mrkGr1Wwhw","children":[{"id":"270","parent":"269","text":"Perla 1: La queja de memoria del paciente vale poco; la del informante vale mucho → sin informante fiable el diagnóstico es endeble","guid":"2GwA82vHRPix4G0oMyZviA","children":[]},{"id":"271","parent":"269","text":"Perla 2: El test de cribado se elige según el paciente → MoCA general, RUDAS baja escolaridad, Mini-Cog si 5 min; MMSE INSENSIBLE para DCL","guid":"d8M05FqNQ9WENActYBze2A","children":[]},{"id":"272","parent":"269","text":"Perla 3: Sumar 1 punto al MoCA si escolaridad <12 años → evita falsos positivos en población chilena","guid":"XtjcMY8lSsqHOYNtU6WAGQ","children":[]},{"id":"273","parent":"269","text":"Perla 4: TSH + B12 son innegociables → causas reversibles simples, dramáticas si corregidas","guid":"zVexOnmsRNC06foAge82iQ","children":[]},{"id":"274","parent":"269","text":"Perla 5: 45-50% de las demencias son prevenibles (Livingston Lancet 2024) → HTA, audífonos, DM, ejercicio, no tabaco/alcohol, educación, prevención TEC; SPRINT-MIND ↓ 19%","guid":"ipNSnP2qTEi9qOYFHa5f0w","children":[]},{"id":"275","parent":"269","text":"Perla 6: El delirium es marcador de cerebro vulnerable → 30% progresan a demencia en 1 año (Inouye 2014); seguimiento cognitivo activo","guid":"gwhMFEYdRWCuYwIfNxkC5A","children":[]},{"id":"276","parent":"269","text":"Perla 7: Pseudodemencia depresiva → sospechar si queja prominente + poco esfuerzo en test; tratar depresión primero","guid":"yZHIMe5VQfmazFn4fJl1JQ","children":[]},{"id":"277","parent":"269","text":"Perla 8: MTA ≥2 en RM en <75a = bandera roja para conversión Alzheimer; Fazekas ≥2 = pequeño vaso activo","guid":"jo45gh-0TaWQ0MkzcsPrQw","children":[]},{"id":"278","parent":"269","text":"Perla 9: \"Regla del año\" DLB vs PDD → cognitivo en 1er año = DLB; ≥5 años después = PDD (importante por hipersensibilidad neuroléptica DLB)","guid":"2MlPxBiNTte_EoH9p1miLA","children":[]},{"id":"279","parent":"269","text":"Perla 10: El cuidador es paciente oculto — aplicar ZARIT desde la 1ª consulta → claudicación = causa principal de institucionalización","guid":"Mlkz32O0S1ua2jgaLeaXGQ","children":[]},{"id":"280","parent":"269","text":"Perla 11: Stepwise approach Altuna 2025 → cribado + FR + neuroimagen + plasma p-tau 217 puede hacerse desde APS, no requiere unidad de memoria para todos","guid":"O4cs6ZfNSdGCF6zjMXhYQA","children":[]},{"id":"281","parent":"269","text":"Perla 12: Cognitive impairment es vital sign cardiovascular (Jamil JACC 2025) → individualizar metas de PA, anticoagulación, estatinas en DCL/demencia","guid":"BheFMnDwReKJGWprCXyt4Q","children":[]}]},{"id":"282","parent":"0","text":"Conceptos examinados (Evaluaciones SGGCh 2026)","guid":"hdnLuDvWSAWQYwzV0N2dFQ","children":[{"id":"283","parent":"282","text":"Evaluacion M2","guid":"Wv7vr4FLR3SnnMOPjI7A1w","children":[{"id":"284","parent":"283","text":"P6 (DCL vs demencia - divisor de aguas): preservacion relativa de AVD basicas + instrumentales (Barthel + Lawton) -> DCL = deficit cognitivo OBJETIVO con AVD PRESERVADAS; demencia = deficit + impacto funcional progresivo (avanzadas -> instrumentales -> basicas). MoCA <26 es screening, no diagnostico; atrofia mesial temporal es soporte no criterio","guid":"mKOhOSlwQsSxT7jX4gSbnQ","children":[]},{"id":"285","parent":"283","text":"P17 (MoCA caracteristicas): 30 puntos maximos, +1 punto compensatorio si escolaridad <=12 anos -> mas sensible que MMSE para DCL (no menos); evalua funciones ejecutivas (Trail B, fluidez, abstraccion); aplicable >80a si lecto-escritura/comprension/sensorialidad preservada","guid":"ixWCozllTvqgc_cKtGox7w","children":[]}]},{"id":"286","parent":"282","text":"Evaluacion Final (transversales)","guid":"trbHPt_RSeCaBzJQS87kag","children":[{"id":"287","parent":"286","text":"No hay items directos para este mapa, pero conceptos de Q6 (DCL/AVD preservadas) y Q17 (MoCA + 1 escolaridad) son fundacionales para el resto del modulo cognitivo","guid":"_MkvqZ-4TnOHTazaBdOqVg","children":[]}]}]},{"id":"288","parent":"0","text":"Referencias (bibliografía oficial Dra. Natalia Nettig)","guid":"Jrtnz0qTTEO6nstlri9o8w","children":[{"id":"289","parent":"288","text":"1. Frisoni GB, et al. New landscape of the diagnosis of Alzheimer's disease. Lancet. 2025;406(10510):1389-1407. doi:10.1016/S0140-6736(25)01294-2","guid":"9PdoY6_kSaWuT91Ov0y0Nw","children":[]},{"id":"290","parent":"288","text":"2. Altuna M, et al. Stepwise approach to Alzheimer's disease diagnosis in primary care using cognitive screening, risk factors, neuroimaging and plasma biomarkers. Sci Rep. 2025;15(1):31526","guid":"Ymda3MMZRhOrVPD5086X9w","children":[]},{"id":"291","parent":"288","text":"3. US Preventive Services Task Force. Screening for Cognitive Impairment in Older Adults. JAMA. 2020;323(8):757-763. doi:10.1001/jama.2020.0435","guid":"mD_VCZOUS_6v7FY_lhEx5Q","children":[]},{"id":"292","parent":"288","text":"4. Goodall LS, et al. Current and Emerging Therapeutic Approaches for Vascular Cognitive Impairment and Dementia. J Am Coll Cardiol. 2026;87(1):77-100","guid":"TxPqxfQyTNW3eAtkTuyxwg","children":[]},{"id":"293","parent":"288","text":"5. Putignano S, et al. Early Detection Screening of Cognitive Decline in Patients Over 60 Years: ELDERCARE Study. J Alzheimers Dis. 2024;98(1):145-150","guid":"PpUTCNEPROODj1AEs4idQA","children":[]},{"id":"294","parent":"288","text":"6. Lazar RM, et al. A Primary Care Agenda for Brain Health: AHA Scientific Statement. Stroke. 2021;52(6):e295-e308","guid":"FffWgz26TPeLKl0b7sx00A","children":[]},{"id":"295","parent":"288","text":"7. Livingston G, et al. Dementia prevention, intervention, and care: 2024 report of the Lancet standing Commission. Lancet. 2024;404(10452):572-628","guid":"lyqxBzVSScWhh88Bvwr7TQ","children":[]},{"id":"296","parent":"288","text":"8. Reuben DB, Kremen S, Maust DT. Prevención y tratamiento de la demencia: Una revisión narrativa. JAMA Intern Med. 2024;184(5):563-572","guid":"k_ZggbdWTwag_HVB55Ojbw","children":[]},{"id":"297","parent":"288","text":"9. McKhann GM, et al. The diagnosis of dementia due to Alzheimer's disease: NIA-AA. Alzheimers Dement. 2011;7(3):263-269","guid":"ORg-naLXRN-kY99CmlxebQ","children":[]},{"id":"298","parent":"288","text":"10. MINSAL Chile. Plan Nacional de Demencia 2017 + Orientaciones Técnicas Guías GES-85 (2019)","guid":"EA0s5jGxR52vNMeT_RlaGA","children":[]},{"id":"299","parent":"288","text":"11. Jamil Y, et al. The Impact of Cognitive Impairment on Cardiovascular Disease. J Am Coll Cardiol. 2025;85(25):2472-2491","guid":"LvxMxz3kTcuEqRuae5eroQ","children":[]},{"id":"300","parent":"288","text":"12. Petersen RC, et al. Mild cognitive impairment guideline. Neurology. 2018;90(3):126-135","guid":"vqvN-CzOT7qP_ibB3Z6dDA","children":[]},{"id":"301","parent":"288","text":"13. O'Brien JT, Thomas A. Vascular dementia. Lancet. 2015;386(10004):1698-1706","guid":"lQyNiA1UR-qsVvLFkdi-jA","children":[]},{"id":"302","parent":"288","text":"14. Ancelin ML, et al. Benzodiazepine use and cognitive decline: The 3-City Study. PLoS One. 2009;4(11):e9099","guid":"svT_Fah2TS-6-14ES3Pv5Q","children":[]},{"id":"303","parent":"288","text":"15. Inouye SK, Westendorp RGJ, Saczynski JS. Delirium in elderly people. Lancet. 2014;383(9920):911-922","guid":"0biLMRX6S1i-gy_uLTXCjA","children":[]},{"id":"304","parent":"288","text":"16. Nasreddine ZS, et al. The Montreal Cognitive Assessment (MoCA). J Am Geriatr Soc. 2005;53(4):695-699","guid":"jnuLiYotS6aNOOS5Tg9QlA","children":[]},{"id":"305","parent":"288","text":"17. Zarit SH, Reever KE, Bach-Peterson J. Relatives of the impaired elderly: correlates of feelings of burden. Gerontologist. 1980;20(6):649-655","guid":"crzpMbOeRUKEEPhVcQNjGg","children":[]},{"id":"306","parent":"288","text":"18. Jack CR Jr, et al. NIA-AA Research Framework. Alzheimers Dement. 2018;14(4):535-562","guid":"OgLfTuB_TcuSOLnsiO9pmg","children":[]},{"id":"307","parent":"288","text":"19. Dubois B, et al. Timely diagnosis for Alzheimer's disease. J Alzheimers Dis. 2016;49(3):617-631","guid":"DMemhNBTRG2iMJoCCzbi7g","children":[]},{"id":"308","parent":"288","text":"20. McKeith IG, et al. DLB consortium criteria. Neurology. 2017;89(1):88-100","guid":"cMw7zewAQ4qWd6Xv9jFNAw","children":[]},{"id":"309","parent":"288","text":"21. Fazekas F, et al. AJR Am J Roentgenol. 1987","guid":"V-shFduGQNK3TP1oCFXZog","children":[]},{"id":"310","parent":"288","text":"22. Wardlaw JM, et al. Neuroimaging standards for research into small vessel disease. Lancet Neurol. 2013","guid":"o6mLxg5RS6SNOv7S0_cZTw","children":[]}]}]},"node_count":310,"relations":[],"cross_references":[],"specialty":"Hematología","folder":"Entidades clínicas/Hematología","filename":"Williams. Anemia hemolítica relacionada con defectos de las enzimas de los eritrocitos-2025","id":"map_165","resolved_references":[]}